WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:10.896
On-chain privacy is hard. Combine UTXOs and you link them, even with CoinJoins. So Fedimix takes a different road: I receive into Fedimint ecash, over time.

00:11.396 --> 00:20.444
Whatever sits above my spending target is split into common denominations and queued. Every coin shows its anonymity set, and how far it has to go.

00:20.944 --> 00:29.920
Then we wait. A coin leaves only when the threshold is reached and the anonymity set is large enough, after a random delay. Timing gives nothing away.

00:30.420 --> 00:41.196
And it exits by itself, straight to cold storage, tagged with its privacy. Anon set seventy-three. Unmixed coins show up in red.

00:41.696 --> 00:46.112
The queue shrinks, the next coin is scheduled, and I do nothing.

00:46.612 --> 00:52.876
Need money right now? Exit early. Fedimix shows the fee and warns me that privacy is lower.

00:53.376 --> 00:58.200
It lands tagged as an early exit, so I always know which coins are less private.

00:58.700 --> 01:07.316
Spending from cold storage? The change does not stay on-chain. It flows back into ecash, as a fresh federation deposit.

01:07.816 --> 01:13.000
Once it confirms, the federation credits the change in Spending. Loop closed.

01:13.500 --> 01:21.564
Spend daily from ecash, with great privacy. Keep the big money on-chain, for maximum self-sovereignty. That is Fedimix.

